\pard\s1\sb240\sa120{\b\fs44 {\f0 \cf1 Demonstration of DOCX support in }{\f0 \cf1 calibre}}\par
\pard\sa120 {\f0 \fs24 This document demonstrates the ability of the calibre DOCX Input plugin to }{\f0 \fs24 convert the various typographic features in a Microsoft Word (2007 and newer) }{\f0 \fs24 document. Convert this document to a modern ebook format, such as AZW3 for }{\f0 \fs24 Kindles or EPUB for other ebook readers, to see it in action.}\par
\pard\sa120 {\f0 \fs24 There is support for images, tables, lists, footnotes, endnotes, links, dropcaps and }{\f0 \fs24 various types of text and paragraph level formatting.}\par
\pard\sa120 {\f0 \fs24 To see the DOCX conversion in action, simply add this file to calibre using the }{\f0 \b \fs24 {\uc0\u8220}Add Books{\uc0\u8221} \b0 }{\f0 \fs24 button and then click {\uc0\u8220}}{\f0 \b \fs24 Convert{\uc0\u8221}. \b0 }{\f0 \fs24 Set the output format in the top right }{\f0 \fs24 corner of the conversion dialog to EPUB or AZW3 and click }{\f0 \b \fs24 {\uc0\u8220}OK{\uc0\u8221}\b0 }{\f0 \fs24 .}\par
\page
\pard\s1\sb240\sa120{\b\fs44 {\f0 \cf2 Text Formatting}}\par
\pard\s2\sb240\sa120{\b\fs40 {\f0 \cf3 Inline formatting}}\par
\pard\sa120 {\f0 \fs24 Here, we demonstrate various types of inline text formatting and the use of }{\f0 \fs24 embedded fonts.}\par
\pard\sa120 {\f0 \fs24 Here is some }{\f0 \b \fs24 bold, \b0 }{\f0 \i \fs24 italic, \i0 }{\f0 \b \i \fs24 bold-italic, \i0 \b0 }{\f0 \fs24 underlined and struck out text. Then, we }{\f0 \fs24 have a super}{\f0 \fs16 script }{\f0 \fs24 and a sub}{\f0 \fs16 script}{\f0 \fs24 . Now we see some red, green and blue text. Some text }{\f0 \fs24 with a yellow highlight. Some text in a box. Some text in inverse video.}\par
\pard\sa120 {\f0 \fs24 A paragraph with styled text: }{\f0 \i \fs24 subtle emphasis \i0 }{\f0 \fs24 followed by }{\f0 \b \fs24 strong text \b0 }{\f0 \fs24 and }{\f0 \b \i \fs24 intense emphasis\i0 \b0 }{\f0 \fs24 . This paragraph uses document wide styles for styling rather than }{\f0 \fs24 inline text properties as demonstrated in the previous paragraph {\uc0\u8212} calibre can handle }{\f0 \fs24 both with equal ease.}\par
\pard\s2\sb240\sa120{\b\fs40 {\f0 \cf3 Fun with fonts}}\par
\pard\sa120 {\f0 \fs24 This document has embedded the Ubuntu font family. The body text is in the }{\f0 \fs24 Ubuntu typeface, here is }{\f0 \fs24 some text in the Ubuntu Mono typeface, notice how every }{\f0 \fs24 letter has the same width, even i and m}{\f0 \fs24 . Every embedded font will automatically }{\f0 \fs24 be embedded in the output ebook during conversion.}\par
\pard\s2\sb240\sa120{\b\fs40 {\f0 \cf3 Paragraph level formatting}}\par
\pard\sa120 {\f0 \fs24 You can do crazy things with paragraphs, if the urge strikes you. For instance this }{\f0 \fs24 paragraph is right aligned and has a right border. It has also been given a light gray }{\f0 \fs24 background.}\par
\pard\sa120 {\f0 \fs24 For the lovers of poetry amongst you, paragraphs with hanging indents, like this often }{\f0 \fs24 come in handy. You can use hanging indents to ensure that a line of poetry }{\f0 \fs24 retains its individual identity as a line even when the screen is too narrow to }{\f0 \fs24 display it as a single line. Not only does this paragraph have a hanging indent, it }{\f0 \fs24 is also has an extra top margin, setting it apart from the preceding paragraph.}\par
