\pard\sa120 {\f0 \fs24 Tables in Word can vary from the extremely }{\f0 \fs24 simple to the extremely complex. calibre tries to do }{\f0 \fs24 its best when converting tables. While you may run }{\f0 \fs24 into trouble with the occasional table, the vast }{\f0 \fs24 majority of common cases should be converted very }{\f0 \fs24 well, as demonstrated in this section. Note that for }{\f0 \fs24 optimum results, when creating tables in Word, you should set their widths using }{\f0 \fs24 percentages, rather than absolute units. To the left of this paragraph is a floating two }{\f0 \fs24 column table with a nice green border and header row.}\par
\pard\sa120 {\f0 \fs24 Now let{\uc0\u8217}s look at a fancier table{\uc0\u8212}one with alternating row colors and partial }{\f0 \fs24 borders. This table is stretched out to take 100% of the available width.}\par
